@startuml

title The Acme demonstration: raising, queueing and deciding an approval

participant "The raiser\n(a trader, or a desk)" as raiser
participant "The decider\n(Operations, Market Risk,\nController, Finance)" as decider
participant "ores.inbox" as inbox
database "the request, its parts\nand its decisions" as db

== A desk raises ==

raiser -> inbox : the owning component's own operation\n(a booking, a book change)
inbox -> db : raise the request: kind, state waiting,\nrequested_by = the raiser
alt the kind asks parts
    inbox -> db : one request-part row for each part\n(controller, finance, market_risk, operations)
    inbox -> decider : a notice to whoever holds\neach part's decide permission
end

== The decider opens the queue ==

decider -> inbox : inbox.v1.ops.list_approval_queue
inbox -> db : the open requests of the kinds\nthis person may decide
note right of inbox
  The queue is filtered by the permission
  each kind names, and the person's own
  requests are cut from the page before
  it is paged. A person never decides
  what they raised.
end note
db --> inbox : waiting and held requests,\nthe raiser's left out
inbox --> decider : the queue, oldest first

== The decider decides ==

decider -> inbox : inbox.v1.ops.decide_approval\n(approve, refuse, hold, resume)
inbox -> inbox : does the caller hold the kind's\nor the named part's decide permission?
alt no
    inbox --> decider : denied, not_a_decider
else yes
    inbox -> db : write the decision\n(decided_by, comment)
    db -> db : the four-eyes trigger refuses\na decision by the raiser
    alt every part approved, or the count reached
        db -> db : state := approved
        inbox -> inbox : the owning component applies it
    else refused, or held
        db -> db : state := refused, or held
    end
    inbox --> decider : the request's state after the decision
    inbox -> raiser : a notice naming the decision
end

== What the demonstration shows ==

note over raiser, db
  The acme_demo seed books each trade as one of
  the party's own traders, so the operational
  authorisation each live trade raises belongs to
  a trader and waits for Operations. Trading
  raises and Operations decides: the two people
  are never the same one.
end note

@enduml
